  "text": "The tutors language model employs a decoder only transformer to process text. A tokenizer divides an input passage into tokens. An embedding layer maps these tokens to numerical vectors. Positional information helps the transformer distinguish sequences containing the same tokens in different orders. Self attention combines information from token representations. A causal attention mask prevents the model from attending to later positions when predicting the next token. Attention connects information across a passage, though models have a finite context window that limits the text available in a single request. Restrictions apply to both training and generation phases. Attention weights do not validate the truth of associated claims.",
